= Commons — Technical =

Common-pool resource analysis distinguishes the resource system from resource units, appropriation from provision, and open access from common property. Institutional outcomes depend on boundary definition, monitoring costs, rule fit, sanctioning, conflict resolution, and interaction across governance levels.

== Modeling cautions ==
* commons ≠ public good
* commons ≠ unowned resource by definition
* commons ≠ inevitable tragedy

== References ==
* Elinor Ostrom, ''Governing the Commons'' (1990).
* Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences, 2009 Prize materials on economic governance and the commons.
* Garrett Hardin, “The Tragedy of the Commons” (1968), as a historically influential model rather than a universal law.
